---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Terminal from '../components/Terminal.astro';
import Code from '../components/Code.astro';
import InstallLine from '../components/InstallLine.astro';
import { FUNCTIONS, CODE_FUNCTIONS, SURFACES, HOWTOS, FACTS } from '../data/catalog.mjs';
import { cell, SURFACE_SAMPLES } from '../data/examples.mjs';

const tabs = [
  { label: 'Bash', alias: 'Bash', surface: 'shell' },
  { label: 'Python', alias: 'Python', surface: 'python' },
  { label: 'TypeScript', alias: 'TypeScript', surface: 'typescript' },
  { label: 'Ruby', alias: 'Ruby', surface: 'ruby' },
  { label: 'R', alias: 'R', surface: 'r' },
  { label: 'Rust', alias: 'Rust', surface: 'rust' },
  { label: 'SQL', alias: 'SQL', surface: 'duckdb' },
];

const jobs = ['decide', 'choose', 'filter'];
const bash = jobs.map((fn) => cell(fn, 'shell').runs[0]);
const surfaceOf = (slug) => SURFACES.find((s) => s.slug === slug);
const plannedCaption = (slug) => surfaceOf(slug).name + ' is planned. This is how the calls will read.';
const sixHowtos = HOWTOS.slice(0, 6);
---
<Base title="ThinkThen">
  <h1>Code that understands.</h1>
  <p class="lede">Ten small functions. Each one asks a question about the evidence and hands back an answer with a probability.</p>

  <h2>Three jobs</h2>
  <p>Answer a yes-or-no question. Pick one option. Keep the records that pass. Change the tab and every code block on the site changes with it.</p>

  <div class="tabbed" data-fallback="Bash">
    <div class="tabs" role="tablist">
      {tabs.map((t) => (
        <button type="button" role="tab" data-lang={t.label} data-alias={t.alias} aria-selected={t.label === 'Bash'}>{t.label}</button>
      ))}
    </div>
    <div class="cell" data-lang="Bash">
      {bash.map((run) => <Terminal run={run} caption="Run against the shipped command and saved." />)}
      <InstallLine line={surfaceOf('shell').install[0][0]} status="planned" note="coming with 0.1" caption="Install the command" />
    </div>
    {tabs.slice(1).map((t) => (
      <div class="cell" data-lang={t.label} hidden>
        <Code code={SURFACE_SAMPLES[t.surface].code} caption={plannedCaption(t.surface)} />
        <InstallLine line={surfaceOf(t.surface).install[0][0]} status="planned" caption="Install, once it ships" />
      </div>
    ))}
  </div>

  <p>This is a classifier you do not train. There is no training step. Ask many questions about one text and the answers come back in parallel. The probability was the training target. Nothing added it afterward.</p>

  <p class="pagelinks"><a href="/install/">Every way to install it</a></p>

  <div class="facts">
    <div class="fact"><b>An exit code your script branches on</b><span>0 is yes, 1 is no, 3 is not sure.</span></div>
    <div class="fact"><b>About a penny for a thousand answers</b><span>1.2 cents for 1,000 short texts, from the live probe.</span></div>
    <div class="fact"><b>A probability on every answer</b><span>You set the bar. The middle goes to a person.</span></div>
  </div>

  <h2>The ten functions</h2>
  <div class="grid">
    {CODE_FUNCTIONS.map((fn) => (
      <a class="tile" href={`/functions/${fn.name}/`}>
        <b>{fn.name}</b>
        <span>{fn.line}</span>
      </a>
    ))}
  </div>
  <p class="pagelinks"><a href="/functions/question-file/">A question is also a small file</a></p>

  <h2>The surfaces</h2>
  <div class="grid">
    {SURFACES.map((s) => (
      <a class="tile" href={`/${s.slug}/`}>
        <b>{s.name} <span class={`status ${s.status}`}>{s.status}</span></b>
        <span>{s.blurb}</span>
      </a>
    ))}
  </div>

  <h2>Six how-tos</h2>
  <div class="grid">
    {sixHowtos.map((h) => (
      <a class="tile" href={`/how-tos/${h.slug}/`}>
        <b>{h.title}</b>
        <span>{h.reader}</span>
      </a>
    ))}
  </div>
  <p class="pagelinks"><a href="/how-tos/">All eleven how-tos</a></p>

  <h2>Why a careful engineer trusts it</h2>
  <p>Every answer carries a probability the model reported. You set the bar, and a band sends the middle to a person. The evidence crosses whole, answers are saved, and nothing else leaves the machine. The <a href="/trust/">trust page</a> lays out the outcomes, the thresholds, the cache, and how to check a question against your own labeled records.</p>

  <h2>What it will not do</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>It writes nothing. A function reads the evidence and answers one bounded question. It never edits, summarises, or composes.</li>
    <li>It decides nothing. ThinkThen judges. Your own code turns an answer into an action.</li>
    <li>It does not chat, and it holds no conversation across calls.</li>
    <li>It does not promise an accuracy. {FACTS.cost.rows[0][0]} is a cost. It says nothing about how often an answer is right. Measure a question against your own labeled records before you trust it.</li>
  </ul>
</Base>
